  "action": "Discovered the actual plan tier on PGS Grove is 'taster', NOT Basic+. Critical finding: taster has a FIXED DAILY allowance, and when it hits 0% ALL models return 402 plan_allowance_exhausted - including the 6 'near-endless floor' models the docs advertised. The docs page describes the floor/banking behavior as belonging to Basic and above tiers ('This tier carries a fixed allowance; Basic and above run on paced usage with banking instead of a fixed cap'). So the near-endless-floor feature does NOT apply to the taster plan the user is on. Confirmed via live API test: all 6 floor models returned 402 at 106.3% daily. Daily resets 2026-11-06 04:08 UTC, weekly at 31.9% with ~92% headroom. Also found the 4th model in the floor list (deepseek-v4-flash base) returns 400 for an unrelated reason (invalid model ID)."
